y is not filed the way other memories are. Under extreme threat, the brain prioritises survival over narrative, so fragments — a smell, a tone of voice, a body position — get stored without a timestamp."}],"$L20"],"$L21"]}]}]]}],"$L22","$L23","$L24","$L25","$L26","$L27","$L28","$L29"]}]]}]
