20:["$","p","When a fragment is triggered later, the body responds as if the event is happening now. That is what makes flashbacks so disorienting: the experience is real, but the clock is wrong.",{"className":"text-base leading-relaxed text-body","children":"When a fragment is triggered later, the body responds as if the event is happening now. That is what makes flashbacks so disorienting: the experience is real, but the clock is wrong."}]
21:["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-3xl border border-line bg-surface p-6","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-serif text-xl text-ink","children":"Symptom mechanics"}],[["$","p","Hypervigilance, startle responses, and numbing are all downstream of a threat-detection system that has raised its baseline. Nothing is broken; the setting is simply stuck on high after it was genuinely needed.",{"className":"mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body","children":"Hypervigilance, startle responses, and numbing are all downstream of a threat-detection system that has raised its baseline. Nothing is broken; the setting is simply stuck on high after it was genuinely needed."}],["$","p","Grounding works by giving the brain unambiguous present-tense evidence — cold water, textured objects, naming the year out loud. Trauma-focused therapy then helps the memory be re-filed with its correct date attached.",{"className":"mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body","children":"Grounding works by giving the brain unambiguous present-tense evidence — cold water, textured objects, naming the year out loud. Trauma-focused therapy then helps the memory be re-filed with its correct date attached."}]]]}]
